WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.609
If you're looking for rumors, spoilers, and
leaks about No Time to Die, you've come to

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:06.320
the right place.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:11.900
Grab your martini and load your Walther PPK,
because here's everything we know so far about

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.440
the next 007 film.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:19.420
Details about No Time to Die have been scarce,
but we do have a very minimal plot description.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.300
Here's how IMDb sums it up:

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.480
"Bond has left active service.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:28.240
His peace is short-lived when his old friend
Felix Leiter from the CIA turns up asking

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:32.570
for help, leading Bond onto the trail of a
mysterious villain armed with dangerous new

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.280
technology."

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:37.300
It's generic, but it does give us some hints
about where the plot could be headed.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:43.140
If this is truly Daniel Craig's final run
as Bond, the "one last job" trope could be

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:43.880
rearing its head.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:49.520
The movie is expected to arrive in theaters
on April 8, 2020, and it'll be directed Cary

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:54.530
Joji Fukunaga, who's best known for helming
Netflix's Maniac and the first season of True

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:55.020
Detective.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:00.860
And the writing team consists of Fukunaga,
Neal Purvis, Robert Wade, Scott Z. Burns,

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:01.959
and Phoebe Waller-Bridge.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:07.660
Like some of the other actors who've played
Bond, Daniel Craig has a complicated relationship

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.400
with the character.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.680
He's been praised for his performances, and
the franchise has made him an international

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.580
superstar and a very rich man.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:19.240
However, the grueling pace and workload of
an international film series has taken a toll

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.200
on him, both mentally and physically.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.020
Craig is no longer a young man, and he's suffered
injuries from working on the Bond films that

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.060
have required surgery.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.200
It also seems that he doesn't necessarily
enjoy playing the role anymore.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:36.060
In a 2015 interview with Time Out London,
he claimed that he would rather slash his

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.980
wrists than play Bond again after Spectre
and that if he did do another Bond movie,

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.620
it would only be for the money.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.320
He certainly wasn't lying about that last
part, as he's reportedly bringing in a whopping

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:50.300
$25 million for No Time to Die.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.740
Hopefully that much cash coaxes out his A-game.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.060
There are a lot of elements that contribute
to making an epic Bond film, and one of the

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.920
most important is a memorable villain.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.420
Great bad guys can make a not-quite-great
007 flick at least entertaining, or they can

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.460
elevate an already good film to legendary
status.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.880
No Time to Die is swinging big with its baddie,
enlisting the services of Rami Malek, fresh

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.100
off his Oscar win for Bohemian Rhapsody.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:23.840
"I will be making sure Mr. Bond does not have
an easy ride of it in this, his 25th outing."

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.459
Considering the uncertain fate of Christoph
Waltz's Blofeld at the end of Spectre, there

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:34.700
is some speculation that Malek will take a
turn as Blofeld himself, possibly as a clone

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.020
or through some sort of surgical alteration.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.099
That is far from confirmed, though, and it
appears that Waltz himself will also be appearing

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:46.359
in the film, so don't count on Malek playing
the iconic villain just yet.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.420
Christoph Waltz may not be the only former
Bond villain set to return in No Time to Die.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:56.659
According to Page Six, Grace Jones was booked
for a small role in the film.

00:02:56.659 --> 00:03:02.209
As fans of the franchise know, Jones previously
played May Day, bodyguard to Chrisopher Walken's

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:06.680
Max Zorin in A View to a Kill and a formidable
physical challenge for Bond.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.920
But she will most likely not be returning
as May Day, as she was completely obliterated

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.780
by an explosion at the end of that film.

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:18.320
Unfortunately, it turns out that Jones was
not on the same page as everyone else on this

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.900
seemingly cursed production.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.560
According to The Sun, the actress reportedly
thought she was being offered a bigger role,

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.600
and she took the small cameo she was actually
given as a bit of a slight.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.940
So it now appears Jones won't be appearing
in No Time to Die after all.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.620
No Time to Die is poised to offer callbacks
to many Bond films of the past, and one of

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:43.460
the most iconic locations in his vast filmography
will appear at the beginning of the story.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:48.440
When the film was announced, executive producer
Barbara Broccoli said that it'll begin with

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:53.320
Bond enjoying retirement in Jamaica, which
the team considers the spy's "spiritual home."

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:59.980
1962's Dr. No, 007's very first cinematic
adventure, featured Jamaica prominently, so

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:04.400
it seems fitting that this new film will see
Bond return to the idyllic setting to try

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.420
to live out a normal life in retirement.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.920
But we know that that will be interrupted
when his old CIA friend, Felix Leiter, comes

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.200
calling to rope him back into the game to
deal with a new threat.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.300
Poor Bond, he just wanted to settle down with
Dr. Swann.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:23.180
Maybe this is why Craig hates the role so
much: he never gets to have nice things.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.840
Major No Time to Die plot points are still
under pretty tight wraps, beyond the fact

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.660
that it begins with James trying to get away
from the spy game in Jamaica.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.160
The Daily Mail has revealed that MI6 has moved
on without him.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:42.320
The agency has given away the 007 codename
to another spy, played by Lashana Lynch, who's

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.800
probably best known as Maria Rambeau in Captain
Marvel.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.310
A source close to the film told The Daily
Mail,

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:53.620
"There is a pivotal scene at the start of
the film where M says 'Come in 007,' and in

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.500
walks Lashana who is black, beautiful and
a woman."

00:04:56.870 --> 00:05:00.680
Lynch has discussed how excited she is for
the role, partly because she is of Jamaican

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.680
descent herself.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.000
"We're able to include them in this British
movie.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:08.740
I'm able to mesh the two cultures, much like
I grew up doing.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.380
I'm Brititsh and Jamaican at the same time."

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:16.240
The Daily Mail source added that Bond, of
course, tries to seduce the new 007, but fails.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:21.590
The introduction of this new 007 is being
attributed to one of the writers, Phoebe Waller-Bridge,

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.380
whose hiring was specifically requested by
Daniel Craig.

